  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nRain chances will decrease during the day on Wednesday as the \nleading shortwave pushes into the Ohio Valley. A cold front sinking \nsouthward through the CWA will keep a low chance (20-30%) for rain \ngoing through the day as subtle disturbances ripple overhead. \nAnother more prominent wave moves through the Middle Mississippi \nValley late Wednesday into Thursday, though guidance varies on the \namplitude of the wave and the position of the front. Both will \nimpact the chance for a round of widespread rainfall. A front in our \nimmediately south of the CWA will lead to the focus for rainfall \nbeing mainly along and south of I-70, while if the front is able to \ndrift well south of the CWA by Wednesday evening, then the focus for \nrainfall will be south of the CWA. Currently the common solution \namong guidance favors the former, with the wave spawning widespread \nconvection along and south of I-70. This is reflected in the \nforecast, which calls for a 60-80% chance for rain in this part of \nthe CWA. \n\nFor Thursday through the weekend, flow will become increasingly \nnorthwesterly in the wake of Wednesday's wave, pushing the cold \nfront well south of the region and ushering in another round of \nrelatively cool air. Upper-level ridging over the western CONUS and \ntroughing over the East Coast will keep the CWA beneath \nnorthwesterly flow through the weekend, continuing our stretch of \ncooler temperatures. While there is not a consensus on anything \nright now, we'll have to watch for embedded disturbances within the \nflow that may bring rain to portions of the area through this part \nof the period.",
